From: Nabeel Sowan <nabeel@vibes.se>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:07:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tderandr: report the RandR primary output as primary, not the
 others

readCurrentDisplayConfiguration() marked the output that RandR reports
as primary as not primary, and every other active output as primary;
the comparison has been inverted since it was written in 2011. With
one output the fallback below marks that output primary anyway, which
hides it. With two, the Displays module ticks "primary" on the wrong
monitor and keeps the wrong one from being dragged, and saving that
arrangement records the wrong output as primary, which applying it
then makes the real one.

Set is_primary only on the output RandR names. With no primary set
at all, no output is marked, and the existing fallback and
ensureMonitorDataConsistency() pick one as before. Profiles saved
before this change keep whatever primary they recorded.

Measured on an Xorg dummy-driver server with DUMMY0 and DUMMY1 active:
with RandR's primary on DUMMY0, readCurrentDisplayConfiguration()
called DUMMY1 primary, and with it on DUMMY1, DUMMY0; with this change
it names the same output as xrandr in both cases, and a lone output is
still primary.
---
 tderandr/libtderandr.cpp | 7 +------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tderandr/libtderandr.cpp b/tderandr/libtderandr.cpp
index 94828e434..7a58e5099 100644
--- a/tderandr/libtderandr.cpp
+++ b/tderandr/libtderandr.cpp
@@ -1343,12 +1343,7 @@ TQPtrList<SingleScreenData> KRandrSimpleAPI::readCurrentDisplayConfiguration() {
 
 				// Determine if this display is primary and/or extended
 				RROutput primaryoutput = XRRGetOutputPrimary(tqt_xdisplay(), DefaultRootWindow(tqt_xdisplay()));
-				if (primaryoutput == randr_screen_info->outputs[i]->id) {
-					screendata->is_primary = false;
-				}
-				else {
-					screendata->is_primary = true;
-				}
+				screendata->is_primary = (primaryoutput == randr_screen_info->outputs[i]->id);
 				screendata->is_extended = screen_active;
 				if (!screendata->is_extended) {
 					screendata->is_primary = false;
